WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.084
Build an evaluation set from real workflows using approved representative data.

00:00:06.084 --> 00:00:13.628
Include common tasks, difficult cases, ambiguous requests, stale sources, permission boundaries, and costly errors.

00:00:13.628 --> 00:00:17.278
Define expected outcomes before reviewing results.

00:00:17.278 --> 00:00:28.229
Measure answer quality, citation support, hallucinations, refusal behavior, structured output, latency, prompt processing, generation speed, memory, temperature, failure rate, and recovery.

00:00:28.229 --> 00:00:32.852
Repeat important tests because model output can vary.

00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:35.529
Test the complete application.

00:00:35.529 --> 00:00:46.480
Retrieval, document parsing, prompts, tools, API limits, authentication, interface state, and logs can fail even when the base model performs well.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.643
Track where the failure occurred.

00:00:49.643 --> 00:00:55.241
Collect user feedback tied to tasks rather than general enthusiasm.

00:00:55.241 --> 00:01:01.324
Did the assistant save time, improve quality, or create review work?

00:01:01.324 --> 00:01:07.895
Preserve examples of false confidence, missing sources, poor formatting, and unsafe actions.

00:01:07.895 --> 00:01:16.899
Model, runtime, driver, document, prompt, and configuration updates need versioning, regression tests, change approval, backups, and rollback.

00:01:16.899 --> 00:01:23.956
Rebuilding an index can change answers even when the model stays the same.

00:01:23.956 --> 00:01:31.986
Monitor availability, queues, resource use, unauthorized access, data growth, stale content, errors, and quality trends.

00:01:31.986 --> 00:01:40.504
Expand users, sources, or automation only when existing workflows are reliable and operational ownership is clear.

00:01:40.504 --> 00:01:48.048
Define service objectives for uptime, latency, quality, support response, backup recovery, and index freshness.

00:01:48.048 --> 00:01:55.591
Objectives make tradeoffs visible and show when the assistant needs capacity, redesign, or retirement.
